jobs.description:
The Project Management Director is responsible for the planning, implementation and supervision of the enterprise's project management system, leading a team of project managers, coordinating key projects and cross-department projects, and ensuring that projects are successfully delivered in accordance with the established time, budget, scope and quality standards.

This position requires coordinating product, technology, operations, finance, sales and other functional teams, establishing standardized project management processes and governance mechanisms, and continuously improving project execution efficiency through risk management, resource allocation and performance analysis.

Core responsibilities

1. Project management system
- Establish and continuously optimize the company's project management standards, processes and methodologies;
- Develop project management policies, templates, processes and best practices;
- Establish project governance, approval and reporting mechanisms;
- Promote the implementation of project management standards in different business teams;
- Improve the overall project management maturity of the enterprise.

2. Project planning and execution
- Responsible for the entire process management of key projects from initiation, planning, execution to delivery;
- Establish project goals, timelines, milestones and delivery standards;
- Monitor project scope, schedule, budget and resources;
- Ensure the project is completed as planned;
-Identify and resolve key issues in project execution in a timely manner.

3. Project Portfolio Coordination
- Coordinate priorities and resource requirements among multiple projects;
- Identify dependencies between projects;
- Coordinate project resource conflicts;
- Adjust project priorities according to corporate strategy;
- Provide project portfolio status and risk analysis to senior management.

4. Cross-department collaboration
- Coordinate product, engineering, operations, finance, marketing and sales teams;
- Establish clear project responsibilities and communication mechanisms;
- Promote cross-department teams to execute according to unified goals;
- Handle resource and priority conflicts between departments;
- Establish project escalation and decision-making mechanism.

5. Project risk management
- Establish project risk identification and monitoring system;
- Monitor project progress, budget, scope and resource risks;
- Establish risk warning and emergency response mechanisms;
- Escalate and report major project risks;
- Promote timely resolution of risks and issues.

6. Budget and resource management
- Develop project resource and staffing plans;
- Supervise the implementation of project budget;
- Optimize the allocation of project personnel, technology and external resources;
- Control project costs;
- Ensure resource commitment is aligned with project priorities.

7. Project performance and data analysis
- Establish project KPIs and project health indicators;
- Regularly analyze project progress, budget and delivery status;
- Establish project management dashboard and senior management reports;
- Identify project execution trends and potential problems;
- Make project optimization suggestions based on data.

8. Team leadership
- Lead project managers and project management teams;
- Responsible for project manager recruitment, training and performance management;
- Establish a project management talent development system;
- Cultivate senior project managers and project leaders;
- Establish a results-oriented project management culture.

Qualifications

Educational background
- Bachelor degree or above in project management, business administration, operations management, engineering, information technology or related majors;
- MBA, EMBA or related master's degree is preferred;
- Certifications such as PMP, PgMP, PRINCE2 are preferred.

work experience
- More than 20 years of experience in project management or related business management;
- More than 15 years of project management team leadership experience;
- Experience in Project Manager, Senior Project Manager, Program Manager or PMO management;
- Experience in managing large, complex or cross-departmental projects;
- Experience in building enterprise-level project management systems is preferred.

core competencies
- Project planning and execution;
- Project portfolio coordination;
- PMO management;
- Cross-department communication;
- Project risk management;
- Budget and resource management;
- Project process optimization;
- Data analysis and performance management;
- Team leader;
- Advanced stakeholder management.

Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
- Project delivery rate on schedule;
- Project budget achievement rate;
- Project scope change rate;
- Project risk resolution rate;
-Project delay rate;
- Project resource utilization;
- Project quality compliance rate;
- Cross-department project collaboration efficiency;
- Project stakeholder satisfaction;
- Project target completion rate.

